WEBVTT

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:03.090
Why did you have to die, Rikiishi?

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:34.050
Why'd you have to die, Rikiishi?

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:06.100
The poppy blooms

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:09.570
a bright red...

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:15.290
The lily blooms...

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:26.310
How should I bloom? I...

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.520
My dreams at night...

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.530
Fifteen, six-

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:56.090
However dark the past...

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:55.290
Why?

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:58.000
Ever since I saw your dead face,

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:02.090
why have I felt like there's a big, black hole in my heart?

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:07.330
And why do I get a feeling like the wind's whistling through it?

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:11.870
Why do I feel this way? Hey, tell me, Rikiishi!

00:04:57.260 --> 00:04:59.520
I fought you with everything I had.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:01.590
And you did the same.

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:03.650
And I lost.

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:06.840
I sunk to the mat for the first time in my life.

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:09.490
But I wasn't bitter about it.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.720
It didn't matter who won and who lost...

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:15.960
We settled the score from our juvie days.

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:20.100
All my grudges against you went away.

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:21.840
I felt refreshed, if anything.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:24.990
That meant that when the match was over,

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:27.920
whether or not you and I still lived,

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:30.740
both of us would be done with it all.

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:33.120
That's what our match meant.

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.890
But... But you...

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:58.330
After you actually went and died, I felt so weary.

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:50.950
Whatever the reason, your death was too sudden.

00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:59.930
You vanished from my life so abruptly...

00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:05.630
Of course, you came into my life abruptly, too.

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:08.360
You were never gentle at all.

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:21.020
It was when I tried to escape from the juvenile prison.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:23.730
It was a bolt from the blue.

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:36.070
Up until then, I'd been fighting the world with just my strength and my guts,

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:39.030
but you gave me a beating I'd never forget.

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:42.380
I'd never really felt I hated someone until then.

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:49.910
You were arrogant, cool, and pretty popular.{"snobby" original tl}

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:52.590
And you were real damn strong on top of that.

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:55.040
You were one step above me in everything I did.

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:57.340
And I just couldn't stand that.

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:09.550
It was a burning hot day in the middle of summer

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:13.780
when you and I first put on gloves and exchanged blows in the ring.

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:54.700
If only that match had ended in a draw,

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:58.830
maybe you wouldn't have died.

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:05.120
<i>This was an accident.</i>

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:09.220
<i>Yabuki's strike to his temple in the sixth round</i>

00:10:09.220 --> 00:10:12.300
<i>and the rope's blow to the back of his head when he went down caused a cerebral hemorrhage.{}{}{}{}</i>

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:16.940
<i>And you could say that his harsh weight loss accelerated his death.</i>

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:35.060
Go to the wilderness!

00:10:35.970 --> 00:10:38.830
I am a boxer.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:46.580
The evening sun glitters upon the dreams of men!

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:51.510
Cry tomorrow!

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:55.550
Today, I am a wolf.

00:10:55.970 --> 00:10:59.950
My own scars...

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:25.590
The morning sun rises upon the hearts of men!

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:24.600
I can hear it, Rikiishi...

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:26.200
I can hear you singing...

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:22.690
That's it. I remember clearly now, Rikiishi.

00:12:22.690 --> 00:12:26.610
I've felt this chilly sensation before.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:35.740
When summer was ending, and patchy clouds started filling the sky,

00:12:36.340 --> 00:12:39.300
you left the juvenile detention center before I did.

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:47.410
As you stood before the giant iron doors of juvie,

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:50.260
you were surrounded by several inmates and guards,

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:51.980
basking in their congratulations.

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:55.540
I was watching from a distance.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:13:00.010
"No way in hell I'd be caught dead seeing off someone like you!"

00:13:00.010 --> 00:13:01.360
That's what I thought, at least.

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:05.830
We had promised each other to settle our score as pros in the ring,

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:08.690
so we didn't have any reason to talk.

00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:10.680
But... But you know...

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:12.680
When the time came for you to leave,

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:14.180
I shouted out to you.

00:13:16.550 --> 00:13:17.190
<i>Rikiishi!</i>

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:24.780
I stopped you in your tracks, but I couldn't say a thing.

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:28.190
I don't know what I wanted to say.

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:36.210
You slapped me on the shoulder

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:37.810
and left.

00:13:45.870 --> 00:13:46.880
<i>Rikiishi!</i>

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:55.390
What was I trying to say?

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:58.400
Looking back on it now,

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:01.270
I was afraid to be apart from you.

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:03.170
I felt lonely.

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:07.500
Ever since, Rikiishi...

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:10.590
I felt that you were the closest...

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:13.740
the closest person to me.

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:42.130
And it... it took me until now to figure it out.

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:45.110
What an idiot I am!

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:25.100
<i>The cause of Rikiishi-kun's death{3-liner, split by editor}</i>

00:15:25.100 --> 00:15:29.100
<i>was Yabuki-kun's blow to his temple in the sixth round...</i>

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:41.840
<i>Yabuki-kun's blow to his temple in the sixth round...</i>

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:44.460
<i>Yabuki-kun's blow to his temple...</i>

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:46.460
<i>Yes. This was an accident.</i>

00:15:47.020 --> 00:15:51.770
<i>An accident...</i>

00:15:51.770 --> 00:15:54.160
No. I...

00:15:55.070 --> 00:15:56.470
With my own hands...

00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:58.970
I killed Rikiishi!

00:15:59.570 --> 00:16:01.490
I killed the man whose place no one could take,

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:03.890
here in the ring.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:07.940
I killed him!

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:26.940
Rikiishi was led to death by his impossible weight loss.

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:30.730
Rikiishi endured shedding pound after pound

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:32.570
just to be in the same bantamweight class as me.

00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:35.050
Because of his big-boned frame,

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:37.060
his weight loss was very severe.

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:40.890
He stopped drinking water,

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:43.350
and only ate one fruit a day, just so that he could fight me.

00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:49.010
It must've been tough, Rikiishi.

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:51.450
I'll never forget

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:56.200
that you risked your own life to keep our promise.

00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:00.330
You really were a great guy.

00:17:01.860 --> 00:17:07.250
And you're the only one who ever took me seriously.

00:17:08.120 --> 00:17:09.590
Joe the Orphan.

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:10.960
Joe the Outlaw.

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:12.190
Joe the Brawler.

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:13.280
Joe the Wild.

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:19.540
For as long as I can remember, everyone in this world

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:24.340
has only tried to engage me from a distance.

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:28.080
Even to old man Danpei,

00:17:28.550 --> 00:17:33.710
I was nothing more than a boxing doll to fulfill his lost dreams.

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:36.670
But... But Rikiishi...

00:17:37.090 --> 00:17:38.780
You were different.

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:41.950
Hey, hey, hey! Sir, sir, sir!

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:44.230
You look awful cold! Why don't you come by for a drink?

00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:46.820
Come on in! We've got some hot oden here!

00:17:46.820 --> 00:17:50.710
Come on, come on! You know you want to! Here, have a seat!

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:52.960
Come on in! Have a seat!

00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:56.670
Hey! We got a customer!

00:17:58.430 --> 00:17:59.180
Welcome, sir!

00:18:02.650 --> 00:18:04.020
Rikiishi Toru...

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:10.190
Rikiishi Toru was the only one who came at me with everything he had...

00:18:10.670 --> 00:18:12.690
So what'll it be, sir?

00:18:13.050 --> 00:18:18.700
And he sacrificed everything, just so we could break each other's bones.

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:21.200
What do you want to eat, sir?

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:25.720
We didn't know each other long, but we were completely intertwined.

00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:29.620
Hey!

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:30.570
What?

00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:32.470
This one ain't answering!

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:35.910
I bet he must've got himself drunk already!

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:38.220
Don't mind him. Just give him something.

00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:47.760
The punches we threw with all our might...

00:18:47.760 --> 00:18:49.600
The blood that spurted and sprayed...

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:55.620
Those spoke of our manly souls far better than a million pretend friendships.

00:18:56.750 --> 00:19:01.940
Yes, to the loner called Yabuki Joe,

00:19:01.940 --> 00:19:05.280
he was like a father, a brother, a best friend...

00:19:06.130 --> 00:19:08.690
and more than that...

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:10.530
He was... He was my everything.{hopefully I alpha'd this right}

00:19:10.530 --> 00:19:11.830
He was... He was my everything.

00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:23.970
Oh, really now?

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:25.440
He did that?

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:28.440
Yeah! And I thought it was so strange...

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:29.160
Fair enough...{added}

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:30.960
Here you are, sir.

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:31.870
Here, here!

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:32.680
Ah, thanks.

00:19:32.680 --> 00:19:34.010
You might as well, right?

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:36.680
I swear, it was strange!

00:19:39.940 --> 00:19:43.550
And yet I killed that person who was special to me.

00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:45.340
What am I supposed to do now?

00:19:45.340 --> 00:19:47.740
Hey, look! He's a crying drunk!

00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:54.920
Well? What's wrong with that? Keep it coming!

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:57.300
From the looks of it, I bet he can keep going!

00:19:57.300 --> 00:19:59.440
Hey, we'd like the bill!

00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:02.760
Yes, coming up! That'll be 18,000 yen.

00:20:03.110 --> 00:20:04.560
18,000?

00:20:04.560 --> 00:20:06.300
That's a joke, right?

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:08.530
We just had two plates of oden and two or three cups of shochu...

00:20:08.530 --> 00:20:11.530
What's the matter? You guys picking a fight?

00:20:11.530 --> 00:20:13.330
Picking a fight? Of course not!

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:15.900
Then come outside, sir.

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:16.880
All right!

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:18.350
So you're a rip-off joint, huh?

00:20:18.350 --> 00:20:20.910
Rip-off? What the hell do you mean by that?

00:20:20.910 --> 00:20:23.320
Just tell us whether or not you're gonna pay up!

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:25.780
<i>This was an accident.</i>

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:27.870
<i>Yes. An accident.</i>

00:20:33.220 --> 00:20:34.410
Now isn't that strange?

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:39.130
I definitely killed him, but I guess killing a man in the ring isn't a crime.

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:46.250
Well, I can't accept that!
I'd rather have committed a crime!

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:49.720
I bet I'd feel a lot better if they'd just thrown me in prison!

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:58.440
Shut up! If you can't pay, we're gonna take your clothes!

00:20:54.650 --> 00:20:57.310
<i>Please, stop it!{added}</i>

00:20:58.440 --> 00:20:59.820
You got that?{added}

00:21:01.610 --> 00:21:05.580
It's a pity for the old man, but I don't feel like getting back in the ring.

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:09.710
But if you take boxing from me, I'm just the scum of the earth.

00:21:05.870 --> 00:21:07.380
<i>Give it back!{added}</i>

00:21:07.380 --> 00:21:08.410
<i>Shut it!{added}</i>

00:21:10.380 --> 00:21:13.810
So it'd be better for everyone else if I were in prison.

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:16.500
Old man... and Nishi...

00:21:17.110 --> 00:21:19.910
I won't be seeing you guys for a while.

00:21:21.160 --> 00:21:24.650
It's too bad for these rip-off oden vendors that happened to be here,

00:21:24.650 --> 00:21:26.430
but I'm gonna beat them to death.

00:21:27.130 --> 00:21:29.430
Murder in the ring may not be a crime...

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:31.440
but murder here is a crime.

00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:35.120
I bet this'll be making headlines in tomorrow's paper.

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:40.020
"Up-and-Coming Boxer Yabuki Joe Causes Another Brawl, Imprisoned for Manslaughter."

00:21:44.620 --> 00:21:46.690
What the hell do you want, fucker?

00:21:49.400 --> 00:21:51.700
Son of a bitch! You laughin' at us?

00:21:58.710 --> 00:22:02.450
Now we're talking! Don't blame me if I kill you, kid!

00:22:02.450 --> 00:22:03.540
Kill <i>me</i>?

00:22:06.780 --> 00:22:07.840
You little shit!

00:22:12.850 --> 00:22:15.290
Don't just scream at me, kid!

00:22:15.290 --> 00:22:17.350
Don't fuck with us, asshole!

00:22:40.360 --> 00:22:42.910
Trying to act tough, were you, motherfucker?

00:22:42.910 --> 00:22:45.010
Well, it ain't bedtime yet!

00:22:45.010 --> 00:22:47.770
Hey. He's already unconscious.

00:22:48.180 --> 00:22:50.380
Christ, what a night!

00:23:50.590 --> 00:23:53.630
Yuke kouya wo

00:23:50.590 --> 00:23:53.630
Go to the wilderness!

00:23:54.720 --> 00:23:57.470
Oira boxer

00:23:54.720 --> 00:23:57.470
I am a boxer.

00:23:58.260 --> 00:24:05.230
Yuuhi ga giragira otoko no yume wa

00:23:58.260 --> 00:24:05.230
The evening sun glitters upon the dreams of men!

00:24:06.940 --> 00:24:10.900
Minna wa kono ore wo nasakemuyo to iu

00:24:06.940 --> 00:24:10.900
Everyone says that I am merciless.

00:24:10.900 --> 00:24:12.940
Tsuki ni hoete hitori

00:24:10.900 --> 00:24:12.940
Howling at the moon alone.

00:24:14.760 --> 00:24:19.160
Oyanashi yadonashi no na mo nai boxer wa

00:24:14.760 --> 00:24:19.160
A parentless, homeless, nameless boxer

00:24:19.160 --> 00:24:22.560
Kusari wo kamikitta Yeah Yeah!

00:24:19.160 --> 00:24:22.560
has bitten off his chains! Yeah, yeah!

00:24:23.770 --> 00:24:26.790
Yuke kouya wo

00:24:23.770 --> 00:24:26.790
Go to the wilderness!

00:24:28.000 --> 00:24:30.500
Oira boxer

00:24:28.000 --> 00:24:30.500
I am a boxer.

00:24:31.630 --> 00:24:38.760
Asahi ga noboru yo otoko no mune ni {removed the Woo, but otherwise japanese is unchanged - Reed}

00:24:31.630 --> 00:24:38.760
The morning sun rises upon the hearts of men!

00:24:41.120 --> 00:24:42.960
Rikiishi is gone.

00:24:44.140 --> 00:24:48.590
Joe is now alone, embracing the late Rikiishi's shadow,

00:24:48.590 --> 00:24:50.130
wandering the twilit town.

00:24:50.880 --> 00:24:55.140
And as Yohko sinks to the depths of despair from losing Rikiishi,

00:24:55.890 --> 00:25:00.520
these two sorrowful people meet in the corner of the bustling city.

00:25:01.010 --> 00:25:06.390
Now, as Yohko and Joe clash with rage and sadness,

00:25:06.390 --> 00:25:08.050
which way is tomorrow!?
